From 47c71321c1a32de07778de4e8f1e3d44fa40e7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:45:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: C-PHY support (backport)

David Heidelberg's "media: camss: Add support for C-PHY configuration on
Qualcomm platforms" v9 (patches 1-9, codeberg.org/sdm845/linux branch
b4/qcom-cphy, 2026-11-02), squashed and rebased onto 7.3:

  csiphy-3ph: Fix lane mask calculation
  csiphy: Introduce PHY configuration
  csiphy-3ph: Use odd bits for configuring C-PHY lanes
  Prepare CSID for C-PHY support
  Initialize lanes after lane configuration is available
  csiphy-3ph: Add Gen2 v1.1 MIPI CSI-2 C-PHY init
  csiphy-3ph: Update Gen2 v1.1 MIPI CSI-2 C-PHY init
  Account for C-PHY when calculating link frequency
  Enable C-PHY where available

Rebase notes: csiphy_init() keeps the 0x1000 register offset for SM8450
(added by the SM8450 CAMSS patch, which the series does not know), and
csiphy_lanes_enable() gets an SM8450 case with the X1E80100 D-PHY table
and no C-PHY table. The hunk for the newer csiphy_stream_on() PHY-options
path does not apply to 7.3 and is dropped (7.3 has no such path).

Co-developed-by: Petr Hodina <phodina@protonmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Petr Hodina <phodina@protonmail.com>
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
